AB  - This article presents an innovative approach to creating virtual imagery through text and speech interfaces for immersive environments (VR/AR/MR). The research focuses on developing and integrating a system that transforms textual descriptions and voice commands into visual images that can be dynamically embedded in virtual and augmented realities. The developed system employs advanced natural language processing and speech recognition methods combined with generative models to create contextually relevant visual elements. Experimental studies have shown significant improvements in the speed and accuracy of virtual object creation compared to traditional modeling methods. The proposed method demonstrates substantial enhancement of user experience and expands interaction capabilities in immersive environments. The research results open new perspectives for developing intuitive interfaces in virtual and augmented reality, while also contributing to the democratization of content creation for immersive technologies. © 2025 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
