TI  - AI-Enhanced Creation of Digital Twins from iPhone LiDAR for Immersive XR Experiences in NVIDIA Omniverse
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of the International Workshop on Intelligent Immersification in the Metaverse: AI-Driven Immersive Multimedia
SP  - 25
EP  - 33
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3728487.3759232
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3728487.3759232
AB  - In a world where digital and physical realities increasingly converge, digital twins must evolve from static visual replicas into intelligent, context-aware systems. This paper presents a next-generation pipeline that combines Neural Radiance Fields (via Nerfacto) with vision-language semantic reasoning to generate richly detailed 3D digital twins that understand their environments—not just render them. Using multimodal inputs such as LiDAR point clouds and RGB images captured from consumer devices like the iPhone 14 Pro Max, our framework jointly refines geometry, optimizes camera poses, and infuses semantic intelligence into the reconstruction process. The resulting twins are exported as OpenUSD assets for photorealistic, ray-traced visualization in NVIDIA Omniverse. Beyond visualization, the system integrates OpenXR and immersive devices like Meta Quest 2 to let users intuitively explore and interact with reconstructed environments—bridging perception, memory, simulation, and spatial design. Experiments confirm that our method delivers state-of-the-art perceptual quality (PSNR, SSIM, LPIPS) in real-time while remaining computationally efficient. By enabling high-fidelity, semantic-rich reconstructions and immersive interaction using accessible hardware, our framework sets a new standard for intelligent digital twin experiences.
