AB  - In the modern information age, digital communication suffers from a deficit in bodily awareness, despite Mehrabian's 7-38-55 rule indicating that body language conveys 55% of meaning. Moreover, our current vocabulary struggles to describe complex bodily phenomena such as proprioception and social proprioception - the awareness of one's own and others' spatial body positioning. Body Oracle is a speculative design project in computational linguistics that introduces an alternative language system consisting of AI-generated hieroglyphic characters representing corporeal and intercorporeal poses, inspired by ancient Chinese Oracle-Bone Inscriptions. These intuitive, cross-linguistic, cross-cultural signs - akin to emojis - aim to expand our capacity to conceptualize, understand, and communicate bodily and inter-bodily experiences. Drawing on linguistic relativity - the idea that language shapes worldview - we propose that these new hieroglyphic signs will function as a sociolinguistic mediator, influencing the collective semantic cognition of bodily awareness. By envisioning an alternative present, Body Oracle challenges us to reconsider how embodied communication could transform our shared understanding. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
