AB  - This study developed a customizable AR glasses museum guide prototype system based on Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) to improve issues such as insufficient interactivity, rigid content, and poor user experience in traditional audio guides. The system is equipped on the J-Reality J7EF Plus AR glasses, which feature a camera and a transparent Si-OLED display, and is deployed on the NVIDIA Jetson Orin Nano, combining YOLOv11 for real-time object detection with the TAIDE large language model optimized for local Taiwanese languages to enable natural language interaction and personalized guidance. Users can perform exhibit recognition and voice inquiries through gesture control, resulting in an immersive interactive experience. Experimental results show that the YOLO model achieved a mAP@0.5-0.95 of 0.884, the TensorRT format reached a maximum inference speed of 39.44 FPS, and the quantized TAIDE model achieved 11.36 tokens/s. The system's performance and stability were validated through testing, demonstrating its application potential in smart museums. Future plans include optimization and collaboration with museums to conduct user testing, further enhancing practicality and experience quality. © 2025 IEEE.
