AB  - The eXRercise Training System offers a novel AIenhanced XR architecture designed to support sustainable and adaptive smart learning ecosystems. Leveraging Large Language Models (LLMs) for natural language-based scenario creation, immersive Extended Reality (XR) environments, and real-time biometric feedback through IoT wearables, it enables trainers to rapidly develop personalized, context-aware training modules without advanced technical skills. This flexible approach supports a range of application domains, including Industry 4.0 workforce training, such as hazardous robotic operations, smart city education for first responders and municipal personnel, and healthcare simulation for stress management and clinical skill development. The paper focuses specifically on the system's performance evaluation within an Industry 4.0 context, demonstrating its effectiveness in safety training scenarios involving complex, high-risk robotic tasks. © 2025 IEEE.
