AB  - This paper presents the design and evaluation of a Virtual Reality-based cinematography training platform enhanced by Generative AI to provide real-time feedback. Developed using Unreal Engine, the system lets students practice lighting, camera angles, and scene composition in simulated environments while receiving real-time GenAI feedback on scene accuracy. A user study with 21 novice filmmaking students showed significant improvement in post-test scores compared to pre-test results. Qualitative feedback highlighted increased confidence, appreciation for AI-driven feedback, and usability challenges. The findings demonstrate the potential of VR and AI to enhance accessibility, and skill acquisition in filmmaking education. © 2025 IEEE.
