AB  - Direct Volume Rendering effectively visualizes region of interests in the volumetric data, by adjusting transfer function (TF). While traditional desktop-based environments rely primarily on mouse and keyboard inputs for interaction, mixed reality (MR) environments support a broader range of interaction modalities. In this paper, we propose Instinctual TF editor (I-TF) that integrates eye gazing and voice commands combined with hand gestures, enabling intuitive interaction. Specifically, we adopt a large language model to maximize the utility of voice interaction. Our I-TF editor can be particularly useful in contexts where manual input is constrained, such as during surgical procedures. © 2025 IEEE.
