AB  - Generative artificial intelligence (AI) is transforming education by introducing both opportunities and challenges. As AI systems become more agentic, critical questions emerge regarding how educational institutions can prepare for and integrate these technologies to enhance learning and teaching in hybrid intelligence environments. This conceptual paper proposes a framework for designing and studying AI agents that stimulate active learning through learner-AI interactions. The framework is structured around three core components: human learning processes, AI learning processes, and a cross-learning loop that facilitates bidirectional interactions between learners and AI agents. To illustrate the framework’s application, we present a case study involving learner-AI interactions in a mixed reality setting, highlighting how such interactions can promote active learning. Our findings provide a basis for understanding the integration of agentic AI in educational contexts and suggest directions for future research on hybrid intelligence. © 2025 Copyright for this paper by its authors.
