UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105032937161?origin=resultslist
AB  - Structural health monitoring (SHM) has become an essential tool for assessing and maintaining the safety, performance, and longevity of civil infrastructure systems, particularly bridges. This chapter provides a compact overview of the latest trends and emerging technologies in SHM. We explore advancements in sensing technologies, including LiDAR, photogrammetry, computer vision, and immersive visualization tools such as virtual reality, augmented reality, and mixed reality. The integration of digital twins and data-driven approaches such as generative artificial intelligence (AI) is briefly overviewed for their role in enhancing SHM capabilities. Special emphasis is placed on addressing data scarcity challenges using a generative AI model, providing structural response data of structural conditions across dissimilar bridges. The chapter concludes by highlighting key findings from such an application, which demonstrate the potential of generative AI to generalize structural health data between different bridge structures, offering significant innovations in SHM applications. © 2026 Elsevier Ltd. All rights reserved.
