AB  - This chapter describes factory 4.0, the digitalized factory. Digitization is an essential component of the factory of the future. The digital revolution brings together digital technologies such as computer science, the Internet, artificial intelligence and, more recently, the generative intelligence that derives from them. Industrial Internet of Things has been applied in the industrial world. These are networks of physical objects and software that work together. Augmented reality consists of superimposing virtual information (images, text, and sounds) on a real system in real time via a computer system. Robots enable operators to free themselves from repetitive, demanding and dangerous tasks. The chapter also describes several key aspects of the industrialization process in its process engineering phase. The safety management system is a mandatory document binding on factory management. The quality management system is another consolidation system. Operators must feel at ease in their factory, regardless of their position. © ISTE Ltd 2025. All rights reserved.
