TI  - A Study on the Design Framework for Interactive Cultural Heritage Games Driven by Generative Artificial Intelligence: Taking Minnan Floral Tiles as an Example
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Virtual Reality and Interaction Design
SP  - 769
EP  - 775
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3820915.3821033
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3820915.3821033
AB  - Cultural heritage is often faced with challenges related to digital transmission, including the cost of producing digital visual materials, stylistic consistency, and the complexity of interactive narratives. Based on the subject of Minnan floral tiles, this paper presents an interactive game design framework for cultural heritage based on generative AI technology, establishing an “conceptualization – visual generation – interactive implementation” workflow. The framework is based on ChatGPT for text-image prompt generation and refinement, as well as Lovart AI for multimodal visual generation. The “style anchor – feature extraction – prompt template” approach is adopted to ensure stylistic consistency. At the same time, ChatGPT is also adopted to aid Unity platform programming, establishing a human-computer collaborative workflow of “operation – error reporting – modification – testing”. To study the immersive experience factors of cultural heritage interactive games, an AHP model is established to test the system based on user experience experiments using SUS and UEQ-S questionnaires. The results show that the system has good usability (SUS=71.5) and positive experience (UEQ-S=+0.68). The study found that generative AI can improve the efficiency of producing digital visual materials while ensuring stylistic consistency for cultural heritage interactive games, providing a reusable design framework for digital heritage dissemination.
