TI  - AI-Driven Spatial Projection Cooking Tutor: ToF-Anchored Registration and Multimodal Step-wise Guidance
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2026 2nd International Conference on Generative Artificial Intelligence and Digital Media
SP  - 140
EP  - 146
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3803730.3803754
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3803730.3803754
AB  - We present an Immersive Holographic Cooking Tutor that delivers situated, step-wise guidance by projecting instructions directly onto the kitchen workspace. The system integrates ToF-based geometric anchoring, a calibrated depth-to-projector mapping for stable spatial alignment, multimodal instruction generation, and lightweight closed-loop feedback to reduce jitter under clutter, specular surfaces, and fast hand/tool occlusions. We evaluate the approach primarily through modeling and simulation with configurable nuisance factors (clutter, material reflectance, motion, and depth noise), and report improved overlay accuracy and stability over ablated variants without ToF anchoring or feedback. These results suggest projection-based, depth-guided tutoring can provide robust in-situ assistance for hands-on cooking tasks.
