AB  - Intelligent Virtual Assistants (IVAs) are advancing with multimodal AI, yet existing systems still struggle with contextual reasoning, emotion awareness, and natural interaction inside immersive environments. This research presents a hybrid IVA framework that integrates speech recognition, emotion analysis, and generative reasoning with a photorealistic 3D avatar for real-time XR interaction. The system combines Azure Cognitive Services for intent classification with a domain-adapted Mistral LLM for deeper contextual understanding, supported by a lightweight vision module for facial emotion detection. A viseme-synchronized avatar rendering pipeline produces lifelike conversational behavior, enabling seamless multimodal interaction through speech, gaze, and expressionsExperimental evaluation shows that the hybrid model improves intent accuracy, response coherence, and user engagement compared to traditional IVA architectures. The results demonstrate that integrating cognitive AI with immersive avatar-based visualization enhances realism and usability in training, technical support, and interactive assistance scenarios. This work provides a scalable foundation for next-generation, emotion-aware virtual assistants capable of delivering more human-like and context-adaptive interactions in XR environments. © 2026 IEEE.
