TI  - AI-Enabled Dynamic Visual Reconstruction of Northern Chinese Island Culture: A Focus on Marine Heritage Dissemination in Changhai County
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Virtual Reality and Interaction Design
SP  - 433
EP  - 438
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3820915.3820981
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3820915.3820981
AB  - In recent years, the rapid development of Artificial Intelligence (AI) has brought profound changes to the digital representation and dissemination of local culture. Northern Chinese islands culture, exemplified by Changhai County, possesses distinctive regional and seasonal characteristics. However, it faces challenges in continuous cultural dissemination due to seasonal dependence, fragmented visual symbols, and the simplification of traditional rituals. This study employs field surveys and AI-enabled dynamic visualization as its research methodology. It explores the practical applications of AI-enabled dynamic visual technologies in the preservation and dissemination of island culture. The study finds that AI can efficiently support the generation of cultural content, unify visual styles, extract key cultural symbols, and enable interactive experiences, thereby facilitating the dissemination of marine cultural heritage. This paper proposes a structurally integrated four-layer framework for the dynamic dissemination of northern island culture. This facilitates year-round accessibility and authentic representation of northern island culture, while offering a systematic approach to combining generative and platform-based dissemination and providing theoretical guidance and practical reference for cultural preservation, reinterpretation, and interactive engagement.
