UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105038709742?origin=resultslist
AB  - Driven jointly by rapid technological iteration and the renewal of educational philosophies, information-based educational technologies have become a core engine of transformation in history education. Traditional history education faces multiple challenges, including the lack of emotional appeal caused by static presentation, the "affluence dilemma"that prevents learners from being physically present at historical sites, and geographical constraints that limit experiential teaching. Virtual reality (VR) technology offers an innovative pathway to addressing these challenges. Taking the practice of history education at the Mogao Caves in Dunhuang as a case study, this paper explores the pathways and practical value of integrating information-based educational technologies with history education. The results show that, supported by core computer technologies such as convolutional neural networks (CNNs) and generative adversarial networks (GANs), platforms including Exploring Dunhuang and Digital Dunhuang have realized 1:1 three-dimensional reconstruction of caves and high-precision replication of murals, enabling immersive and interactive learning experiences. Validation through linear regression and multilayer perceptron (MLP) neural network analyses demonstrates that these technological innovations effectively break through temporal and geographical constraints, enhance the attractiveness and dissemination efficiency of history education, and contribute to the living inheritance of the millennia-old Dunhuang culture. This paper further analyzes the key advantages and existing problems of technological applications and proposes optimization strategies, such as deepening technological integration and establishing ethical norms. These findings provide practical references for promoting the deep integration of VR technology and history education, constructing a new "experiential"model of history teaching, and supporting history education in fulfilling its fundamental mission of fostering virtue through education. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
