AB  - Global population ageing presents dual challenges: the growing demand for physical care and the need for mental health support. AI-driven elderly care systems have made progress in physiological monitoring, but emotional well-being interventions remain underexplored. This paper proposes BatiX, an emotion-adaptive Artificial Intelligence Agent (AI Agent) system that integrates Large Language Models (LLMs) with Extended Reality (XR) technology. BatiX achieves real-time perception of elderly users' emotional states by fusing multimodal information. The system continuously tracks emotional, behavioral, and physiological signal changes over time, supporting intervention evaluation and adjustment. Traditional Batik Art from China and Malaysia serves as visual intervention content, featuring specific fractal complexity and color valence. This research adopts XR as an age-friendly delivery medium, designing a dual-output mode combining "VR immersive experience + projection mapping." This approach effectively covers elderly populations with varying degrees of disability, from healthy individuals to bedridden patients. BatiX offers an innovative pathway for elderly mental wellness in the ambient intelligence era, merging Intangible Cultural Heritage (ICH) with emotion-adaptive regulation. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
