AB  - Negotiation is a key skill in everyday consumption and workplace communication. However, most existing negotiation training tools rely on text based interfaces and rule driven scripts, providing limited situational context and insufficient support for practicing complex negotiation processes. To explore more context aware training approaches, we develop a Unity based virtual night market negotiation platform. The system consists of three core modules. A user preference modeling module estimates pricing preferences and concession tendencies from user inputs, historical bidding records, and interaction level cues, including linguistic style features and facial expression related visual indicators derived from image processing. An environmental factor modeling module represents predefined scene level variables such as noise level, crowd density, lighting conditions, visual distractions, and time constraints as contextual factors relevant to negotiation. A strategy selection and language generation module integrates user related and environment related factors within a unified framework to produce dynamic vendor pricing and context appropriate verbal responses. Dialogue generation in the system is supported by a large language model to simulate diverse negotiation styles for training purposes. © 2026 IEEE.
