AB  - Selecting perfume is often a challenging task that relies on fleeting impressions, making it difficult for customers to compare scents or articulate their preferences. In this paper, we present a data-driven co-creation system that integrates virtual reality (VR), scent-delivery installations, electroencephalography (EEG) data, and artificial intelligence (AI) generated cards with augmented reality (AR) support to transform the concrete experience into a quantified assessment for perfume-making. In this Fragrance Journey, users explore the scenario-based VR environment to sample scents, providing explicit ratings while the system simultaneously captures EEG-derived features. These physiological indicators are converted into weighted metrics, which an algorithm uses to synthesize high-scoring components across fragrance notes into a personalized formula, and then visualized as a unique AI-generated card to get perfume profiles for follow-up customization. The proposed design integrates digital contexts with physical olfactory stimuli, offering a novel paradigm that would contribute to the customization of scent products. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
