AB  - Generative Artificial Intelligence (Generative AI) and Augmented Reality (AR) have garnered increasing attention from researchers for their application in the field of education. Investigating how to integrate Generative AI in a visual way into real classrooms is one of the directions for the deep integration of information technology and science education in the future. This study designed and developed an AR-based embodied conversational agent (ECA) Virtual Scientist and explored its impact on students’ learning outcomes and experience. A total of 62 primary school students participated in a four-week experiment, in which the quantitative and qualitative data were collected to be analyzed through covariance analysis and thematic analysis. It is found that the intervention of the AR-based embodied conversational agent significantly enhanced students’ critical thinking, inquisitiveness and learning motivation. Moreover, students positively evaluated the technology. This study provides experience and strategies for the development and practical classroom application of Generative AI-based AR learning environment, offering practical guidance for the implementation of human–computer teaching. © 2025 Informa UK Limited, trading as Taylor & Francis Group.
