AB  - Building Information Modeling (BIM) technology has been increasingly applied in landscape design. However, traditional BIM methods still face limitations in modeling complex landscape elements and design optimization. Deep learning provides a novel approach to address these challenges. This study proposes an integrated method combining BIM and deep learning for visualized landscape design and optimization. A convolutional neural network-based model is constructed for landscape element recognition, along with a generative adversarial network framework for design scheme generation. Experimental verification based on a city park project shows that the proposed method achieves a recognition accuracy of 94.235%, improves design generation efficiency by 67.892%, and yields a user satisfaction score of 4.726 out of 5, demonstrating its effectiveness and practical value in the landscape design domain.
