AB  - This paper presents a locally hosted, intelligent Virtual Reality (VR) platform that comprehensively evaluates and enhances both soft skills and technical competencies while guaranteeing complete data privacy. The system integrates immersive VR simulations with AI-powered conversational agents that dynamically adapt questioning difficulty based on the user's real-time responses, using a Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) approach backed by a local ChromaDB vector database. Built entirely on open-source technologies - Ollama, Whisper, Piper TTS, and Rhubarb Lip Sync - the platform operates on-premise without any third-party cloud dependency. The key contributions are threefold: (1) a Multimodal System Design Interviewer employing Llama 3.2 Vision to perform cross-modal verification of virtual whiteboard diagrams against spoken justifications, achieving 88.4% component identification accuracy; (2) a Multi-Agent Group Discussion module with parallel n8n-orchestrated AI personas and asynchronous real-time scoring; and (3) a secure, Docker-containerized multi-language coding environment supporting the 'Think Aloud' protocol. Behavioral analysis is achieved through Google MediaPipe for head pose and eye gaze tracking, combined with Three.js ray casting for gaze validation in the 3D environment. Experimental results on consumer-grade hardware (RTX 4090) demonstrate interactive latency under 8 seconds for core assessment modules, validating the platform as a cost-effective and privacy-preserving training tool for educational institutions. © 2026 IEEE.
