AB  - Advancements in multimedia technology enable remote exploration of cultural heritage sites, with Virtual Reality (VR) allowing users to visit historical sites virtually. Utilizing digitized data from the Dunhuang Research Academy, a VR experience of the Dunhuang Caves offers structured tours or self-directed exploration, each with distinct challenges. To address this, we developed an assistive guiding system integrating a virtual agent powered by Microsoft Azure and ChatGPT, providing interactive guidance and knowledge. A user study on Dunhuang Cave 61 examined the impact of virtual agent appearances and behaviors, revealing that full-body agents with gestures and expressions provide the most realistic and engaging presence. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2026.
