AB  - We present Taste as Form, a mixed reality system that translates eating sensations into real-time generative visual structures. The system integrates vision-based food analysis to infer taste, texture (mouthfeel), and color, synchronized with sEMG sensing of chewing dynamics. Taste inputs determine geometric form and color palettes, while texture cues dictate material physics and motion behavior. The visual animation is driven by the user’s real-time chewing rhythm, which modulates the onset, intensity, and decay of the effects. This work proposes a framework for structuring taste and texture as computational interaction signals to generate real-time interpretable visual feedback for immersive dining experiences.
