AB  - Digital transformation and the increasing use of generative AI in higher education amplify the need to emphasize reflective and process-oriented learning. Portfolios are well-established instruments for promoting such learning, yet conventional electronic portfolios (e-portfolio) remain largely two-dimensional, even when maintained as multimodal portfolios. This paper proposes the XR Portfolio as an immersive, social, extended-reality (XR) space that functions as the portfolio medium, combining findings from immersive learning research and reflective learning studies. A pilot implementation in a master-level course explored its feasibility and pedagogical potential. Preliminary findings suggest that XR Portfolios enhance spatial communication, foster deeper reflection, and encourage professional identity development. The study outlines design implications, technical considerations, and directions for further research on assessment and scalability. © 2026 IEEE.
