AB  - In this work-in-progress paper, we present a concept of an AI-powered VR training system that leverages a synthetic audience - an adaptive population of generative agents to deliver real-time, emotionally grounded feedback to speakers. Operating in token time, multimodal interaction tokens from the presenter update agent-level affective states and a population-level resonance field, which in turn generates coherent audience reactions. Unlike traditional VR systems that only measure human responses passively, our closed-loop, co-adaptive design transforms audience feedback into an active training signal by simulating social resonance through generative audience models. The framework establishes a bidirectional learning loop in which speakers and audiences adapt together to optimize social communication performance. For learners, the synthetic audience enables on-demand, repeatable practice with lifelike reactions and automated feedback, accelerating skill acquisition. For training providers, it scales delivery without synchronous facilitators, lowers per-session cost, and yields standardized analytics for program improvement. © 2026 IEEE.
